LOCAL STORAGE

Inspect all localStorage and IndexedDB usage.

Check:

- Whether important records are stored only locally.
- Whether browser storage failures are handled.
- Whether application updates preserve existing records.
- Whether storage keys conflict.
- Whether malformed data can break the application.
- Whether storage operations are versioned where needed.
- Whether sensitive information is stored unnecessarily.
- Whether data can be recovered after a failed update.

If records exist only in local storage, do not silently
delete them or migrate them destructively.

Design and test a safe migration path when required.

CLOUD PERSISTENCE

If a cloud database is used, verify:

- Successful creation and retrieval of records.
- Correct user ownership.
- Authorization enforcement.
- Consistency after refresh.
- Consistency after logout and login.
- Correct behavior across two authenticated devices.
- Failure handling when the network is unavailable.
- Recovery after connectivity returns.
- Protection against duplicate writes.
- Appropriate database indexes.
- Safe query limits and pagination.
- Correct handling of concurrent modifications.

Do not claim multi-device synchronization works unless
it has actually been tested.

BACKUP AND RESTORE

Implement or repair a safe backup and restore workflow
when supported by the current architecture.

Requirements:

- Provide an explicit backup format.
- Validate backup contents before restoration.
- Validate schema versions.
- Detect malformed or incompatible backups.
- Preserve a recoverable copy before destructive changes.
- Prevent duplicate record creation during repeated restores.
- Detect conflicting records.
- Preserve record ownership.
- Preserve transaction identifiers.
- Preserve historical dates and timestamps.
- Report imported, skipped, conflicting, and failed records.
- Make repeated imports safe where feasible.
- Never silently overwrite newer records.
- Never silently discard existing local data.

Use deterministic conflict-resolution rules.

If conflicts cannot be resolved safely, report them rather
than guessing.

Where practical, support export and import of user-owned
records in a documented format.

Test backup and restoration using synthetic test data.

